<title>GERMANY: German Nov trade surplus falls from Oct.</title>
<headline>German Nov trade surplus falls from Oct.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator (bln marks):</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  Nov 96   Oct 96	  Nov 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		 +9.8    +11.1	   +10.0</p>
<p> Current account	     +0.2    - 1.3	   + 0.6</p>
<p> Exports			 70.6     74.9	    67.0</p>
<p> Imports			 60.8     63.8	    57.0</p>
<p> Services			-4.0     -4.7	    -3.0</p>
<p> Wage and property income  -1.2     -2.9	    -1.1</p>
<p> Transfers		     -4.5     -4.9	    -4.8</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 +0.1     +0.1	    -0.5</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC Jan-Nov 96     Jan-Nov 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		  +90.5	     +79.0</p>
<p> Current account		-23.5	     -25.2</p>
<p> Exports			  718.5	     686.1</p>
<p> Imports			  628.0	     607.1</p>
<p> Services			 -51.2	     -51.2</p>
<p> Wage and property income   -12.9		+0.5</p>
<p> Transfers			-48.0	     -50.8</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	   -1.9		-2.7</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
